Feature: Developer commands belong to the dashboard registry
  Scenario: Historical input folders do not retain IDE configuration
    Given the ten formerly tracked ticket launch configuration files
    Then those configuration files are absent
    And the retained command tokenizer helper has no editor launch checker
    And authored reports and remaining input scripts are preserved

  Scenario: IDE generation cannot return through command routing
    Given neutral build targets and dashboard owner declarations
    Then editor launch generation targets and public APIs are absent
    And authoring persists build owner declarations without editor output
    And native dashboard run, build and daemon targets remain available

  Scenario: Source regressions remain independent of editor configuration
    Given the current test owner and typed tool declarations
    Then source and registration tests read neutral metadata
    And synthetic parser paths and hostile input rejection vectors remain unchanged

  Scenario: Setup and root infrastructure retain only current headless controls
    Given canonical AGENTS instructions and current neutral build owners
    When setup instruction aliases and root asset contracts are inspected
    Then Claude is the only generated instruction alias
    And root tests do not require removed Cursor or VS Code MCP files
    And Rust boundary tasks depend on neutral owner declarations

  Scenario: Build inputs retain neutral developer control contracts
    Given the .NET build policy and the architecture course project
    When their named source inputs are inspected
    Then .NET source and project inputs include current build and cache policies
    And no removed IDE solution, launch or task configuration is required
    And the course retains its dashboard registry schema input

  Scenario: The canonical dashboard bootstraps its own missing installation
    Given native dashboard commands with or without an installation record
    When the ordinary repository build entry receives commands or help
    Then native commands reach the dashboard launcher with the original mode and control
    And native help is not consumed by generic build help
    And build, compile, install, test and backend scheduling selections retain ordinary routing
    And a nonzero native exit remains a failed invocation

  Scenario: Shared developer tooling resolves canonical provider versions in every installation scope
    Given the root canonical PostCSS and resizable-panel provider declarations
    When the shared UI consumer and all six current lock scopes are inspected
    Then the consumer declares the same exact canonical versions
    And each current lock selects that same provider version
    And a nested consumer provider takes precedence over a conflicting top-level lock entry

  Scenario: Unknown ignored IDE controls cannot return outside known owners
    Given conventional IDE names and language-neutral physical and manifest vectors
    When the no-follow authored workspace census excludes external and generated caches
    Then every authored IDE directory, workspace, solution and editor launch file is refused
    And arbitrary manifest executable and input references are refused
    And negative input exclusions, passive extensions and historical documents are preserved

  Scenario: Editor-specific names are distinguished from ordinary build and passive assets
    Given unknown ignored owners with CMakeSettings, C++ editor properties, Emacs, Vim, Kate and Sublime configuration
    When the physical classifier and independent SQLite name selection inspect them
    Then those editor controls are refused even when the configuration is a symlink
    And ordinary CMake presets and passive code snippet assets remain accepted
